{#
	Renders a project carousel from committed screenshot or video files.
	One carousel slide per entry, all images and videos must be in the repo.

	Screenshots: { desktop, mobile, alt }
	`desktop`/`mobile` are local screenshots (1440x810 and 600x1200 viewports)
	rather than fetched from a live URL at build time. These <img> tags still
	pass through eleventyImageTransformPlugin to be optimized (e.g. webp/avif)

	Videos: { video, poster, alt }
	Videos render as a single landscape <video>, as it is visible enough on mobile
	and desktop, unlike the portrait screenshots the desktop/mobile split exists for.
	No autoplay, `preload="none"` means nothing is fetched until they press play on
	the native controls, and `poster` gives them the screenshot experience until then.
#}
{% macro websiteCarousel(pages) %}
<div class="carousel-container">
	<div class="carousel">
		{% for page in pages %}
		<div class="carousel-slide">
			{% if page.video %}
			<video playsinline controls preload="none" poster="{{ page.poster }}" aria-label="{{ page.alt }}">
				<source src="{{ page.video }}" type="video/mp4">
			</video>
			{% else %}
			<picture class="screenshot-desktop">
				<img{% if not loop.first %} loading="lazy"{% endif %} src="{{ page.desktop }}" alt="{{ page.alt }}">
			</picture>
			<picture class="screenshot-mobile">
				<img loading="lazy" src="{{ page.mobile }}" alt="{{ page.alt }}">
			</picture>
			{% endif %}
		</div>
		{% endfor %}
	</div>
</div>
{% endmacro %}
